  "notes": "Modified cash basis statements. Governmental figures use the Total Governmental Funds column (p6, left half on p5); Nutrition Fund is business-type (pp7-8). Interfund transfers: Total column eliminates the 90,000 General-to-Depreciation transfer (receipt and pupil transportation spending both removed, Pupil transportation 139,551 = 229,551 - 90,000); the 34,358 General Fund transfer to Nutrition remains in the printed total disbursements 5,999,785, so it is recorded as transfers_out and excluded from disbursements (included via includes). Support services Other 341,950 split into Depreciation Fund 122,350 and Activity Fund 219,600 (student activities) from the fund columns. Federal programs, state categorical programs and special education counted as instruction. Pro-rate, homestead, property tax credit, ESU, state aid counted as state aid; carline, public power district, nameplate as other taxes. Business-type measure is net position (equals cash; no liabilities); beginning 115,308 and ending 69,116 printed on p8. Identity checks: gov 2,908,697 + 6,440,963 - 5,965,427 - 34,358 = 3,349,875; nutrition 115,308 + 153,534 - 234,084 + 34,358 = 69,116. Beginning cash for governmental is the Aug 31 2024 total fund balance (all cash). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p9) used for General Fund (the statement is fund-column only); General Fund detail receipts include non-revenue receipts, expenditure total 5,098,812 includes the 34,358 and 90,000 transfers (recorded as other financing outflows with a 90,000 contra in pupil transportation). Depreciation Fund receipts total 92,622 includes the 90,000 transfer. Student activity detail comes from the Activity Fund column only (no per-account schedule in trimmed pages). Read pages 1-13 of 13"
